{#- The director's tie-break over a simultaneous turn's conflicting actions (FR-MULTI-8; #175).

Under ``simultaneous_tie_break = director`` a turn whose primaries acted on one object at once asks
the narrator once who got there first. The ``system`` block holds the rating guidance (always
first, FR-RATE-4), the custom instructions, the scenario text, the director's notes (the
narrator's context alone, FR-SCN-11), the scene, the last beats as the narrator perceives them
(``think`` excluded), each contested object with the conflicting ``say``/``do`` actions only, and
the tie-break contract. The ``user`` block is the player input. The answer is the call's
``response_schema`` (``{adjudications: [{object, winner}]}``): one winner per object, among the
characters who acted on it. -#}
{% macro line(entry) -%}
{% if entry.text %}{{ entry.text }}{% else %}{{ entry.name }}:{% if entry.say %} "{{ entry.say }}"{% endif %}{% if entry.do %} *{{ entry.do }}*{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
